      },
      "text": "Photography is **controlled light capture** — physically recording photon interactions with matter, then interpreting that record. The history is a sequence of progressively more sensitive, more stable, and more computationally tractable recording media."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#003",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:photography:00-overview, git-history:photography:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "photography/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "photography/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:photography:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "photography",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "photography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Photography - Overview",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nERA         RECORDING MEDIUM            KEY INNOVATION\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n1021        Pinhole + paper             Camera obscura (Ibn al-Haytham)\n1826        Bitumen on pewter           Heliograph: first photograph (Niépce, 8h exposure)\n1839        Silver iodide on silver     Daguerreotype: unique positive, no negative\n1841        Silver bromide on paper     Calotype: negative → multiple positives (Talbot)\n1851        Collodion on glass          Wet plate: sharper, faster — must develop wet\n1871        Ag-Br gelatin on glass      Dry plate: store before/after exposure\n1888        Ag-Br gelatin on paper roll Kodak roll film: democratization of photography\n1925        35mm leica miniature        35mm standard: portability, large print from small neg\n1935        3-layer dye-coupled film    Kodachrome: color reversal, archival stability\n1970        Silicon photodiodes         CCD invention (Boyle & Smith, Bell Labs)\n1975        Digital prototype           Kodak digital camera: 0.01MP, cassette output\n1991        Kodak DCS-100               First commercial DSLR: 1.3MP on Nikon F3 body\n2007        iPhone + computational      Multi-frame processing, AI pipeline, social share\n2016+       Neural rendering, AI        Upscaling, style transfer, generative photography\n```"
    },
